      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Evinston was part of the 1817 Arredondo Grant, a large Spanish land parcel that once covered much of central Florida.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evinston%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A devastating freeze in 1895 ended orange cultivation in Evinston, shifting the local economy away from citrus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evinston%2C_Florida",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Evinston sits on the west shore of Orange Lake, offering scenic views of the water and surrounding wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evinston%2C_Florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community straddles two metro areas: the Gainesville Metropolitan Statistical Area in Alachua County and the Ocala area in Marion County.",
